{"task": "IG-2B04", "path": "src/wgc/sources/README.md", "start_line": 1, "lines": ["# Independent source inventory (wgc-inventory-1)", "", "This lasting tooling implements physical source accounting and evidence locators.", "The schema is `contracts/ig/regions.schema.json`; `inventory.validate` checks shapes,", "canonical hashes, identity references, complete pages, geometry, coverage partitions,", "reading order and evidence bytes. It reuses the frozen IG-1A integer-only canonical", "JSON and offline schema evaluator without changing their bytes. This sidecar does", "not create or approve source-IG semantic records. IG-2 reconciliation must bind these", "exact locators to source-IG regions and preserve the frozen IG-1A review rules.", "", "## Identity and revisions", "", "A source has a logical source ID and exact PDF SHA256. A persisted registry assigns", "UUIDs to explicit page and region keys. Page keys are physical page addresses within", "one exact PDF revision, spelled `physical-page:<1-based number>`. Validation refuses", "another physical address under that key/UUID. Region keys are author-assigned and never derived from text,", "coordinates, content hashes or array positions. Replaying the registry retains IDs;", "reordering or editing a region changes its revision, not identity. Retired registry", "entries remain available. Splits/merges require new explicit keys and a later lineage", "decision. A new PDF SHA256 refuses automatic registry reuse: page correspondence must", "be resolved explicitly, so inserting a page cannot silently transfer identity.", "", "Revisions are SHA256 of WGC-C14N-1 bytes excluding only the enclosing `revision` field.", "Nested records carry their own revisions. Inventory hashes include the persisted", "registry and exact evidence references; timestamps/cost/runtime measurements are", "operational sidecars. New output directories are mandatory; no overwrite or promotion.", "", "## Page geometry and labels", "", "`pdf_page` is 1-based physical order. Printed labels are independent: unknown has", "null plus reason; embedded PageLabels is unverified metadata; verified requires a", "separate exact evidence ID. Absence of PageLabels never implies the printed number.", "Verified label evidence must belong to that same physical page and remain current;", "checking that association does not verify the visible glyph or a human's identity.", "", "MediaBox and CropBox serialize native bottom-left PDF coordinates in integer", "micro-points. One native unit is UserUnit/72 inch. Effective CropBox is their positive", "intersection. Reject nonpositive boxes/units and unsupported rotations. Canonical", "region boxes are unrotated effective-CropBox top-left **integer page millionths**,", "with x right, y down, and half-open bounds. Regions must fit this frame; no silent", "clipping. `pdf_to_box` converts native PDF bounds with outward rounding; `box_to_pdf`", "returns exact rational native bounds. UserUnit cancels in normalization and scales", "physical dimensions. `display_box` applies clockwise /Rotate (0/90/180/270); displayed", "dimensions swap at 90/270. No mixed text/box denominator conventions are inferred.", "", "Evidence derives a separate PDF with MediaBox/CropBox set to the exact region and", "UserUnit scaled into its content and geometry. It preserves page rotation. Poppler", "renders that cropped page; pdfplumber clips extraction to the same displayed frame.", "Text, PNG and cropped PDF each have repo-relative safe path, byte count and SHA256.", "Text offsets use Unicode codepoints and half-open bounds in the exact UTF-8 file.", "Text extraction order is not reading order. Empty text can be valid for a diagram;", "its presence or absence never grants coverage. Evidence includes original source,", "region revision, page, box, engines/versions, DPI and pixel dimensions. Its required", "`page_basis_hash` pins page ID/key, physical address, source revision, both PDF boxes,", "effective crop, rotation and UserUnit, excluding mutable labels and evidence. This", "coverage-independent basis prevents circular hashes and invalidates stale geometry.", "The evidence identity includes that basis. Uncertainty is separate. Revisions, source", "or artifact changes invalidate the evidence locator. Existing evidence without the", "basis requires new derivation in a new output directory; do not invent a freshness pin.", "", "Poppler pixel dimensions use the ceiling of each displayed physical crop axis in", "points times DPI/72, evaluated at double precision. UserUnit scales both axes, and", "90/270 rotation swaps them. Validation checks this prediction against metadata and", "the actual PNG header, with no one-pixel tolerance. It never rounds to nearest.", "", "`validate(document, root)` reopens the byte-pinned PDF, compares strict pypdf and", "Poppler page counts, and verifies every physical page's actual geometry. Both counters", "inside edited JSON cannot conceal an omitted PDF page. It rechecks the PDF pin after", "validation. This is structural access only, with no text/image extraction. Validation", "without `root` checks internal consistency and reports source structure as unverified;", "it cannot substantiate a claim about actual source bytes.", "", "## Order, links and coverage", "", "An explicit global reading-order list names each region once. It can describe columns", "and cross-page order; no top-to-bottom extraction heuristic approves it. Typed", "`continuation`, `note_for` and `illustrates` links retain exact region IDs and a reason.", "Links describe structure, not executable dependencies or accepted interpretations.", "", "Inventory boxes on each page must be disjoint. Duplicate IDs/keys and overlaps fail."], "truncated": true}

